  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warmer and more humid conditions return this weekend \nwith at least periodic chances for some showers and scattered \nthunderstorms Saturday afternoon through Sunday.\n\nA weak secondary cold front will push south through the western \nSouthern Tier with just the chance for a few isolated showers there \nthis afternoon. Otherwise, high pressure will build over the region \nwith dry, cooler, and less humid conditions through the end of the \nwork week.\n\nSurface high pressure will move east into New England, with a \nsoutherly return flow advecting a warmer and more humid airmass back \nin across western and northcentral NY from southwest to northeast \nthrough the day Saturday. This may lead to some scattered diurnally \ndriven convection across western NY Saturday afternoon, particularly \nacross the interior Southern Tier where the best moisture will be, \nalong with somewhat better forcing closer to a mid level shortwave \npassing by just to our southeast. A cold front will then cross the \narea sometime on Sunday...timing is still in question. This will \nbring the next best chance for a round of showers and scattered \nstorms. At this point wind shear and instability both appear to be \nmodest, thus the severe threat looks low at this time. However, if \nthe frontal timing comes across the area at/near peak heating, the \nthunderstorm potential could be greater. Will continue to monitor.",
